In article <Nov.3.13.23.41.1989.14969@topaz.rutgers.edu> linhart@topaz.rutgers.edu (Mike Threepoint) writes:
>(a) Open/closed/no doors will have different symbols in Patchlevel 6.

Good.  (Locked?)

>(b) If you could open doors by walking into them, you'd hardly be aware of
>    them.  Visibly different symbols obviate most of the bother.

I see no problem with being hardly aware of doors.  Doors add
something to the game; having to use a separate command and watch the
screen for the result to open them does not.

A door is basically a simple-minded bear trap.  There *could* be a
seperate command which you'd have to apply over and over to get out of
a bear trap.  There isn't, because it would be as annoying as hell.
Same thing for doors.  When you run into a door you should attempt to
open it; when your Control-Run into a door you should attempt to open
it until you are successful (max of 25 tries, say).  Get rid of "o
<dir>".

BTW, I am the Scott Turner of fountain/Kop/magic trap/etc. fame.  I
was a little unhappy with Nethack 3.0's treatment of Kops.  I intended
them to be rather light-hearted and not a really deterrent to thieving
shops (which I think is a fine thing).  In the version of Nethack I'm
using (which may be HARD) they're damn tough and don't seem to run
around randomly much.

